    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27393" root="طوى" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَاوٍ</span></b>  A gazelle <i>that bends,</i> [or <i>is bending,</i>] or
<i>has bent, his neck, on the occasion of lying
down, and then lies down,</i> or <i>has</i> [<i>lain down
and</i>] <i>slept free from fear.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَاوِى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الكَشْحِ</span> <i>Rendered lean</i> or <i>lank; not large in the
sides.</i> (Ham p. 495.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also the paragraph
commencing with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَوِى البَطْنِ</span>.

